2 projects target several frameworks (src/Dahomey.Json.Tests/Dahomey.Json.Tests.csproj, src/Dahomey.Json/Dahomey.Json.csproj).
Run 'bro format' instead of 'dotnet format' here: with IDE0055 on, 'dotnet format' crashes on multi-targeted
projects (Roslyn can't merge the target frameworks' copies of a file). The command runs it once per target framework.
Wrote the built-in rule severities to .editorconfig.
Set the preset version in Directory.Build.props (<StyleBroPreset>1.0</StyleBroPreset>): rules of newer releases stay off until you raise it.
Note: /home/user/stylebro/.trials/Directory.Build.props is above the repository, and MSBuild reads only the nearest Directory.Build.props: the new one hides it (it isn't imported, since another checkout doesn't have it). If your build needs it, import it from the new file.
To report them on build too: <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild> in Directory.Build.props.
Tip: --agents-md writes a StyleBro section into AGENTS.md for AI coding agents.
